# TypeScript — Data, Types, Utils

## `app/data/`

- Colocate interface + constants in the same file (`Project` in `projects.ts`, `SkillGroup` in `skills.ts`).
- Site-wide copy/config: `siteConfig` in `site.ts` (`as const` when appropriate).
- Consumers import from `~/data/<module>` — not from deep relative paths.

```ts
// ✅
import { siteConfig } from '~/data/site'
import type { Project } from '~/data/projects'

// ❌ duplicate ad-hoc project shapes in components
```

## `app/types/`

- Thin re-exports only (`export type { Project } from '~/data/projects'`).
- Prefer defining new domain types next to their data module; re-export if widely shared.

## `app/utils/`

- Pure helpers with focused names (`parsePostsPage`, `formatPostDate`, `resolveNavRoute`).
- Export named constants used by pages (`POSTS_PER_PAGE`, `POSTS_HOME_PREVIEW`).
- No Vue component logic here — keep SSR-safe and side-effect free.

## Editing content

- New portfolio projects → append to `projects` array (required fields: `slug`, `title`, `company`, `role`, `duration`, `summary`, `contributions`, `tags`, `image`).
- Skills → `skillGroups` / `skillLinks` in `skills.ts`.
- Nav/brand strings → `siteConfig` in `site.ts`.
